The vm80a core (1801BM1/vm80a, CC BY 3.0) is not part of this repository. The waveforms it reads come
from vm80a_sim in the retrocpu-tools release named in scripts/retrocpu.pin, which embeds vm80a
unmodified and carries its notice and licence text.

hwfrp (TheCBaH/coralview) and Rivet (TheCBaH/rivet) are MIT-licensed dependencies installed as opam pins.

workloads/upstream/ holds verbatim copies of third-party 8080 sources with their licences and
the ports in (workloads/lib/ackermann.ml, mul16.ml, div32x16r.ml) translate them to OCaml
builder calls: Rosetta Code's Ackermann function (GNU Free Documentation License 1.2) and litwr2's
rosetta-pi-spigot (GNU General Public License 2.0). Those files keep their own licences, named in their headers
and in workloads/upstream/PROVENANCE.md.

Everything else in this repository is under the MIT License in LICENSE.md.
